---
import DetailLayout from "../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---
<DetailLayout seoTitle="Guilin on Your China Trip - Guilin Yangshuo Guide" title="How to Fit Guilin Into Your China Trip" subtitle="Multi-city routes with flight times, train connections, and where Guilin fits in the classic China circuit."
  description="How to fit Guilin and Yangshuo into a multi-city China itinerary: flight times, train connections, and 3 sample routes that make the detour worth it.">
  <h2>The Classic China Circuit</h2>
  <p>Most first-time visitors follow a route like: Beijing (Great Wall, Forbidden City) -> Xi'an (Terracotta Warriors) -> Guilin/Yangshuo (karst scenery) -> Shanghai (modern China). Guilin fits perfectly as the nature-and-recovery segment between the intensity of Beijing/Xi'an and the urban energy of Shanghai.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-12">Connection Times</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm border border-stone-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
      <thead class="bg-stone-50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">
        <tr><th class="px-4 py-3">From</th><th class="px-4 py-3">To Guilin by Air</th><th class="px-4 py-3">To Guilin by Train</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-100">
        <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Beijing</td><td class="px-4 py-3">3 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~10 hours (high-speed)</td></tr>
        <tr class="bg-stone-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Xi'an</td><td class="px-4 py-3">2 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~8 hours</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Shanghai</td><td class="px-4 py-3">2.5 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~9 hours</td></tr>
        <tr class="bg-stone-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Guangzhou</td><td class="px-4 py-3">1 hour</td><td class="px-4 py-3">2.5 hours (high-speed)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Hong Kong</td><td class="px-4 py-3">1.5 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-3">3.5 hours (via Shenzhen)</td></tr>
        <tr class="bg-stone-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Chengdu</td><td class="px-4 py-3">1.5 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~7 hours</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-12">Sample Multi-City Routes</h2>
  <h3>Route A: The Classic (10 Days)</h3>
  <p>Beijing (3 days) -> Xi'an (2 days) -> Guilin/Yangshuo (3 days) -> Shanghai (2 days). Fly between cities; the Beijing-Xi'an leg is also a nice high-speed train ride (4.5h).</p>

  <h3>Route B: The Southern Loop (7 Days)</h3>
  <p>Hong Kong (2 days) -> High-speed train to Guilin (3.5h) -> Guilin/Yangshuo (3 days) -> Fly to Chengdu (2 days, pandas + Sichuan food). Great if you're flying into Hong Kong.</p>

  <h3>Route C: Nature & Culture (10 Days)</h3>
  <p>Shanghai (2 days) -> Fly to Guilin -> Guilin/Yangshuo (3 days) -> Fly to Lijiang -> Yunnan (4 days: Lijiang, Tiger Leaping Gorge, Shangri-La). Best for nature lovers who want China's two most scenic regions in one trip.</p>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">Booking Strategy</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-stone-700">Book domestic flights 2-4 weeks ahead for the best prices (typically $80-150 per leg). High-speed train tickets open 15 days before departure — set a reminder. For the Guangzhou-Guilin train (2.5h, the most convenient), book as soon as tickets open during peak seasons.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400">Continue Reading</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
      <li><a href="/china-trip-builder/" class="text-accent hover:underline">China Trip Builder</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guilin-to-yangshuo/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Guilin to Yangshuo Transport</a></li>
      <li><a href="/china-visa/" class="text-accent hover:underline">China Visa Guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guilin-yangshuo-itinerary-3-day/" class="text-accent hover:underline">3-Day Itinerary</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</DetailLayout>


